<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Weissenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1296 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Weißenburg in Bayern</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Franconian imperial city on the old Roman frontier that governed itself as a free city until 1802.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weissenburg-in-bayern">Weissenburg</a> lies beside the Roman fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biriciana">Biriciana</a> on the Raetian limes. A Carolingian royal estate stood there, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne's</a> attempted canal between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> basins, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fossa-carolina">Fossa Carolina</a>, lay nearby. The town was a royal possession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> and by the end of the 13th century counted as a free imperial city.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> governed the town and its small territory. Its economy rested on crafts, traffic on the road from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-augsburg">Augsburg</a> and the stone quarries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconian-jura">Franconian Jura</a>. The city adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Lutheran Reformation</a> and belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconian-circle">Franconian Circle</a>. Above it stood the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wulzburg">Wülzburg</a> fortress, held by the margraves of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-brandenburg-ansbach">Principality of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, its constant rivals.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weissenburg-in-bayern">Weissenburg</a> was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1802 and formally annexed in 1803 under the mediatisation of the imperial cities. It is now Weißenburg in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Bayern</a>, known for its Roman baths and a hoard of Roman treasure found there in 1979.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-imperial-city-of-weissenburg.jpg" alt="Free Imperial City of Weissenburg" width="320" height="387"><figcaption>Image: wuppertaler · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GER_Wei%C3%9Fenburg_in_Bayern,_Altes_Rathaus_0010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1296 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Weißenburg in Bayern</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>East Franconian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Weißenburg in Bayern</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1549&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-weissenburg" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Weissenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4933 467 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Weissenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5253 723L5229 694M5253 723L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5253 723h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5253 723h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1549&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-weissenburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
